 "prompt": "The repository at /testbed has a bug, described below. Fix it by changing the source code; do not modify or\nadd tests. When you are done, the project's existing test suite should pass.\n\n<issue>\nDialect.get_or_raise fails to parse dialect settings with key-value pairs\n\n#### Description\n\nWhen using `Dialect.get_or_raise()` with dialect strings that contain key-value pairs (e.g., `'mysql,normalization_strategy=lowercase'`), the method fails to properly parse and apply the settings. The dialect object is created but the specified settings are not applied.\n\n#### Steps/Code to Reproduce\n\n```python\nfrom sqlglot.dialects.dialect import Dialect\n\n# This should create a MySQL dialect with lowercase normalization strategy\nmysql_dialect = Dialect.get_or_raise('mysql,normalization_strategy=lowercase')\nprint(f\"Expected: LOWERCASE, Got: {mysql_dialect.normalization_strategy}\")\n\n# This should create an Oracle dialect with specific settings\noracle_dialect = Dialect.get_or_raise('oracle, normalization_strategy = lowercase, version = 19.5')\nprint(f\"Expected settings: {{'version': '19.5'}}, Got: {oracle_dialect.settings}\")\n\n# This should handle boolean settings properly\nbool_dialect = Dialect.get_or_raise('oracle, s1=TruE, s2=1, s3=FaLse, s4=0, s5=nonbool')\nprint(f\"Expected: {{'s1': True, 's2': True, 's3': False, 's4': False, 's5': 'nonbool'}}\")\nprint(f\"Got: {bool_dialect.settings}\")\n```\n\nThe dialect objects are created successfully, but the key-value settings specified in the dialect string are not being parsed or applied to the resulting dialect instance.\n</issue>\n",
